<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Aerial photograph showing an insulator string on a power line, with insets highlighting two close-up views labeled \215No_issues\216 and \215notbroken-notflashed\216 indicating intact insulator components for inspection purposes.) /K 349 0 R /P 50 0 R /Pg 9 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
301 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Flowchart illustrating a two-stage deep learning pipeline for insulator defect classification. Stage one uses a YOLO detector to localize insulators in training images, extracting patches with bounding boxes for further processing. Stage two applies lightweight MobileNetV3 as a patch-level classifier, augmented with data, outputting probabilities for four classes: no issues, glaze flashover damage, not broken but not flashed, and shell broken. Loss functions include cross-entropy loss for classification and hard-pair contrastive loss for distinguishing class zero from class two, with total loss calculated as a sum of these components. Classes are defined visually with sample images.) /K 350 0 R /P 50 0 R /Pg 10 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
302 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Collage of six photographs showing power line insulator strings, each highlighted with color-coded boxes around the insulators and their components. Backgrounds include vegetation and earth, indicating outdoor settings. Each insulator string is attached to metallic transmission structures.) /K 351 0 R /P 50 0 R /Pg 11 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
303 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Six-panel comparison of insulator fault detection outcomes using three methods: Cascade R-CNN, YOLO11n, and Proposed \(Two-Stage\). Each panel displays power line insulators labeled with colored boxes indicating shell broken \(red\), no issues \(green\), glaze flashover damage \(yellow\), and not broken-not flashed \(blue\). The bottom contains a legend specifying box color meanings.) /K 352 0 R /P 50 0 R /Pg 12 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
304 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Comparison of power line insulator detection methods using aerial imagery, presented in a three-by-four grid. Each row shows a different insulator scenario. The first column displays original color sample images, followed by three columns showing visualization of detection heatmaps from DCS-Attn, YOLO11n, and a proposed two-stage method. The proposed method highlights insulators with more focused and consistent results compared to the other models.) /K 353 0 R /P 50 0 R /Pg 13 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
